WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.000
Let's follow the path of Dusty's trail, oh Dusty's trail, Dusty's trail

00:08.000 --> 00:16.000
A stage and a wagon ahead and west, part of a wagon train lost from the rest

00:16.000 --> 00:24.000
Dusty's the reason for their flight, thanks to Dusty nothing's right

00:24.000 --> 00:32.000
Only the wagon master's hand keeps them rolling through the promised land

00:32.000 --> 00:37.000
All that going gets mighty rough but they don't seem to mind

00:37.000 --> 00:43.000
It's California, eh, that's the place they must find

00:43.000 --> 00:51.000
Deserts and rocks are in their way but they won't stop come what may

00:51.000 --> 00:56.000
Mountains and hills that they must scale but they know they'll make it

00:56.000 --> 01:04.000
Cause they just can't fail on Dusty's trail

01:04.000 --> 01:23.000
Hey little doggie, just hold still cause I'm gonna rope and tie ya

01:34.000 --> 01:50.000
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa

01:50.000 --> 01:54.000
Please don't whoa, please don't whoa, please don't whoa, whoa, whoa

01:54.000 --> 01:58.000
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

01:58.000 --> 02:00.000
Mr. Callahan, look what I caught.

02:00.000 --> 02:02.000
More like he caught you.

02:02.000 --> 02:03.800
It's more like he caught you.

02:03.800 --> 02:05.160
She's really a beauty, isn't she?

02:05.160 --> 02:06.680
A genuine Appalachian.

02:06.680 --> 02:08.840
It's not an Appalachian, it's Appaloosa.

02:08.840 --> 02:10.720
And it's not a she, it's a he.

02:10.720 --> 02:12.040
I don't care if it's a boy Appaloosa

02:12.040 --> 02:13.680
or a girl Appalachian, it's a beauty.

02:13.680 --> 02:15.040
Sure is.

02:15.040 --> 02:16.440
Can I keep him?

02:16.440 --> 02:17.920
Looks like a wild horse.

02:19.080 --> 02:20.160
And those shoes.

02:23.560 --> 02:25.160
Don't see any sign of a brand.

02:26.320 --> 02:28.520
Looks like you found yourself a horse, Dusty.

02:28.520 --> 02:29.680
Really?

02:29.680 --> 02:31.600
It's my own horse and I can keep him?

02:31.600 --> 02:32.600
My own horse.

02:33.920 --> 02:36.960
Don't fight, I'll see if I can get you out of this.

02:36.960 --> 02:38.720
You get in some of the wildest.

02:38.720 --> 02:40.040
Don't let go.

02:40.040 --> 02:41.200
Let go of this one.

02:42.520 --> 02:43.360
Let go!

02:54.640 --> 02:57.520
Just like your Appaloosa cut off here, you're right.

02:57.520 --> 02:58.840
With them other tracks.

02:58.840 --> 03:01.120
I told you it was a horse thief, Marshal.

03:01.120 --> 03:02.360
Keep your rope handy, Roy.

03:03.320 --> 03:04.920
As soon as we catch up with him,

03:04.920 --> 03:07.360
we're gonna hang that barbara to the nearest tree.

03:25.840 --> 03:29.000
And it's not exactly the governor's mansion.

03:29.000 --> 03:32.760
Oh no, but it'll sure be nice to sleep inside for one night.

03:33.680 --> 03:35.640
That corral's in pretty good shape.

03:35.640 --> 03:39.240
I'd be happier with that information if I were a horse.

03:39.240 --> 03:42.360
This place looks like it's the rest home for termites.

03:42.360 --> 04:02.800
Carter, why is everything out west so western?

04:02.800 --> 04:05.480
Hey, look everybody, I caught myself a wild horse.

04:07.480 --> 04:09.160
Doctor, he's beautiful.

04:09.160 --> 04:11.320
Oh, me, he's a beauty.

04:11.320 --> 04:12.720
I'm gonna call him Freckles in that county

04:12.720 --> 04:14.800
that's got all those freckles.

04:14.800 --> 04:16.400
No, those are called blotches.

04:16.400 --> 04:18.520
Yeah, I'm still gonna call him Freckles.

04:18.520 --> 04:19.920
I don't like the name blotch.

04:19.920 --> 04:22.360
He is an elegant looking beast, isn't he?

04:22.360 --> 04:24.240
Yeah, of course, you're a pretty piece of change

04:24.240 --> 04:25.920
to buy one like that.

04:25.920 --> 04:29.720
Please, I've never invested anything that eats.

04:29.720 --> 04:32.160
I'm not gonna sell him, I'm gonna keep him forever.

04:34.160 --> 04:35.440
It may take you that long to break him.

04:35.440 --> 04:36.880
He looks a little ornery to me.

04:36.880 --> 04:38.640
I can be just as ornery as he is.

04:38.640 --> 04:39.960
I just need a little practice.

04:39.960 --> 04:41.760
Well, I'm afraid we haven't got time, Dusty.

04:41.760 --> 04:43.880
We're gonna pull out of here at sunup tomorrow.

04:43.880 --> 04:47.560
Good, the accommodations here are simply dreadful.

04:47.560 --> 04:50.400
Hey, Mr. Callahan, guess what?

04:50.400 --> 04:51.800
I found a telegraph in there.

04:51.800 --> 04:54.960
Oh boy, a telegraph, I mean a real telegraph.

04:54.960 --> 04:56.200
What's a telegraph?

04:56.200 --> 04:59.160
It's a new invention by Samuel Morse.

04:59.160 --> 05:00.680
You see that wire?

05:00.680 --> 05:02.360
You can send messages over it.

05:02.360 --> 05:04.120
You gotta be joshing me.

05:04.120 --> 05:06.440
You can't send messages over a skinny little wire like that.

05:06.440 --> 05:08.240
You know where you can fit?

05:08.240 --> 05:09.080
Yes, you can.

05:09.080 --> 05:12.400
You send it by clicking a series of dots and dashes.

05:14.520 --> 05:16.600
That invention is gonna make millions.

05:18.760 --> 05:19.800
What's the matter with him?

05:19.800 --> 05:20.960
Nothing.

05:20.960 --> 05:22.360
He always cries when he hears

05:22.360 --> 05:24.040
of someone else making millions.

05:25.600 --> 05:27.920
Anyone, I figure if I can repair the break in the wire,

05:27.920 --> 05:30.000
I can make contact all the way back to St. Louis.

05:30.000 --> 05:32.200
Oh good, we can find out where we are.

05:32.200 --> 05:33.720
And where to go.

05:33.720 --> 05:36.360
How long you think it'd take you to fix that contrast?

05:36.360 --> 05:38.000
Couple of days, maybe three.

05:38.000 --> 05:40.920
Oh great, then I can bring freckles while we're waiting.

05:40.920 --> 05:42.280
There.

05:42.280 --> 05:44.800
And then you'd have your very own horse, Dusty.

05:44.800 --> 05:47.800
Yeah, my very own horse.

05:47.800 --> 05:50.360
Me and freckles, together forever.

05:50.360 --> 05:53.280
Looks like your horse needs to join the wagon train, Uriah.

05:53.280 --> 05:55.560
Yeah, yeah, come on, let's move, Marshall.

05:55.560 --> 05:58.840
I don't want him crossing any borders before we hang in.

05:58.840 --> 05:59.680
Okay.

05:59.680 --> 06:02.560
["The

06:10.560 --> 06:12.600
Wagon of the World"]

06:12.600 --> 06:14.640
Wow, that makes 17 times as hit the ground,

06:14.640 --> 06:15.800
according to my count.

06:15.800 --> 06:16.640
I counted 18.

06:16.640 --> 06:17.960
You're both wrong, it's 20.

06:17.960 --> 06:20.000
You forgot the time he bounced twice.

06:20.000 --> 06:22.640
Come on, Dusty, get up on him again, boy.

06:22.640 --> 06:49.360
["The Wagon of the World"]

06:49.360 --> 06:52.520
Hey, Dusty, why don't you quit for a while?

06:52.520 --> 06:53.800
I think he's tired.

06:53.800 --> 06:55.680
You think he's tired, huh?

06:55.680 --> 06:57.720
He's not throwing me as far as he was before.

06:57.720 --> 06:59.440
All right, Dusty, I'm gonna show you something

06:59.440 --> 07:00.880
about breaking a horse.

07:00.880 --> 07:03.960
The first thing you got to do is show him who's boss.

07:03.960 --> 07:06.160
He knows that, he knows that.

07:06.160 --> 07:08.120
Come on, come on.

07:08.120 --> 07:11.640
["The Wagon of the World"]

07:11.640 --> 07:15.320
Mr. Jones, Bean, Bean, and Springfellow, stop.

07:16.480 --> 07:19.920
By one million shares of Eerie Barge.

07:19.920 --> 07:20.760
Stop.

07:20.760 --> 07:21.680
Mr. Brookhaven.

07:21.680 --> 07:23.440
Even if I repair this telegraph key,

07:23.440 --> 07:26.040
I must use it for more important messages than that.

07:26.040 --> 07:27.960
More important than money?

07:29.320 --> 07:31.720
If you're not joking, young man, you're sick.

07:31.720 --> 07:58.760
["The Wagon of the World"]

07:58.760 --> 07:59.600
Hey.

07:59.600 --> 08:04.600
["The Wagon of the World"]

08:04.600 --> 08:08.320
Oh, feels just like I slipped and fell in the bathtub.

08:08.320 --> 08:10.920
Look, it is a bathtub.

08:10.920 --> 08:12.000
Well, I'll be...

08:12.000 --> 08:14.160
I wonder why anyone would leave it here.

08:14.160 --> 08:16.880
Yeah, well, too heavy to carry on a stagecoach.

08:16.880 --> 08:19.600
Yeah, they probably busting an ax or getting a disc for it.

08:19.600 --> 08:21.400
Are you thinking what I'm thinking?

08:22.840 --> 08:26.040
A hot bath, a hot bath.

08:26.040 --> 08:28.080
Hey, how about that, Dusty?

08:28.080 --> 08:29.880
Nice hot bath.

08:29.880 --> 08:31.280
It's not big enough for all of us.

08:31.280 --> 08:32.840
No, no, separately, will you, pal?

08:32.840 --> 08:33.680
Separately.

08:33.680 --> 08:35.000
Girls, go heat up some water.

08:35.000 --> 08:36.200
Right away.

08:36.200 --> 08:38.000
Yeah, come on.

08:38.000 --> 08:39.640
Right, right on.

08:39.640 --> 08:40.480
Knees tight.

08:46.480 --> 08:47.440
Oh, Marshall.

08:47.440 --> 08:49.480
Yeah, it makes that old relay station up ahead.

08:49.480 --> 08:52.640
Uh-huh, so does our horse these tracks.

08:52.640 --> 09:09.640
Get that rope ready, Roy.

09:09.640 --> 09:10.600
Hurry with the hot water.

09:10.600 --> 09:12.600
My goosetops are getting bigger than the sofa.

09:12.600 --> 09:15.600
Now, don't be frightened, Freckles.

09:15.600 --> 09:17.400
I'm not going to hurt you.

09:17.400 --> 09:20.400
Question is, are you going to do the same?

09:20.400 --> 09:21.400
OK.

09:29.400 --> 09:31.200
Easy, boy, easy.

09:31.200 --> 09:32.200
Easy, easy.

09:32.200 --> 09:33.200
Easy, easy.

09:33.200 --> 09:34.200
Easy, easy.

09:34.200 --> 09:35.200
Easy, easy.

09:35.200 --> 09:36.200
Easy, easy.

09:36.200 --> 09:37.200
Easy, easy.

09:37.200 --> 09:38.200
Easy, easy.

09:38.200 --> 09:39.200
Easy, easy.

09:39.200 --> 09:40.200
Easy, easy.

09:40.200 --> 09:41.200
Easy, easy.

09:41.200 --> 09:42.200
Easy, easy.

09:42.200 --> 09:44.400
This is your friend.

09:44.400 --> 09:45.400
Easy.

09:45.400 --> 09:46.400
This is your friend.

09:48.400 --> 09:49.400
Dusty!

10:02.400 --> 10:03.400
Whoa!

10:03.400 --> 10:04.400
Whoa!

10:04.400 --> 10:11.400
Whoa!

10:11.400 --> 10:41.200
You ought to be ashamed of yourself, acting like a wild animal.

10:41.200 --> 10:44.200
Just wanted to be your friend.

10:44.200 --> 10:45.200
Some friend you turned out to be.

10:45.200 --> 10:49.200
OK, I'm not going to put up any more horses around, even our horse.

10:49.200 --> 10:51.200
Do you understand?

10:51.200 --> 11:13.200
Huh?

11:13.200 --> 11:14.200
You did it, Dusty!

11:14.200 --> 11:15.200
You gentleed him.

11:15.200 --> 11:17.200
Yeah, you showed him, booze boy.

11:17.200 --> 11:20.200
Dusty, you're a man after my own heart.

11:20.200 --> 11:22.200
I can't believe it.

11:22.200 --> 11:23.200
My own horse.

11:23.200 --> 11:27.200
My really own horse for the rest of my life.

11:27.200 --> 11:31.200
Course, that won't be for very long.

11:31.200 --> 11:33.200
Welcome to the hangin', folks.

11:40.200 --> 11:43.200
There's some strong trees over by that relay station, Marshal.

11:43.200 --> 11:45.200
Why don't we hang them over there?

11:45.200 --> 11:47.200
Just a minute, Dusty did not steal that horse.

11:47.200 --> 11:48.200
You're right, he's innocent.

11:48.200 --> 11:50.200
You'll have to prove otherwise.

11:50.200 --> 11:51.200
Well, that's easy.

11:51.200 --> 11:53.200
This horse is circle-o stock.

11:53.200 --> 11:56.200
He's only got one mark on him and it's mine.

11:56.200 --> 11:58.200
And there it is, circle-o.

11:58.200 --> 12:02.200
Well, I've looked at a lot of brands, but I never saw that circle before.

12:02.200 --> 12:04.200
Well, that horse has always been covered with spots.

12:04.200 --> 12:07.200
First time I saw him, I thought he had measles.

12:07.200 --> 12:09.200
He's a lowdown horse thief and we're going to hang him.

12:09.200 --> 12:10.200
Now, hold on.

12:10.200 --> 12:12.200
They're extenuating circumstances.

12:12.200 --> 12:15.200
Constable, you must not allow this to happen.

12:15.200 --> 12:19.200
Or the United States government will not receive another penny of my tax money.

12:19.200 --> 12:21.200
But you're supposed to be a lawman.

12:21.200 --> 12:24.200
What kind of justice do they have in this territory?

12:24.200 --> 12:25.200
Okay, okay.

12:25.200 --> 12:27.200
We'll give them a fair trial.

12:27.200 --> 12:28.200
Now, that's better.

12:28.200 --> 12:30.200
And then we'll hang him.

12:31.200 --> 12:32.200
Order of the court.

12:37.200 --> 12:38.200
How long have you known the defendant?

12:38.200 --> 12:40.200
Since we left the East.

12:40.200 --> 12:43.200
In your personal opinion, would he ever steal anything?

12:43.200 --> 12:44.200
No, never.

12:44.200 --> 12:45.200
See, I'm innocent.

12:45.200 --> 12:46.200
Sit down.

12:47.200 --> 12:50.200
I haven't even got to the part about you stealing horses yet.

12:50.200 --> 12:54.200
Do you believe that Dusty would go around stealing horses?

12:54.200 --> 12:58.200
Your Honor, Dusty wouldn't steal honey from a beehive.

12:58.200 --> 13:01.200
There's two things I wouldn't steal, horses and honey.

13:01.200 --> 13:02.200
Sit down.

13:03.200 --> 13:06.200
Marshall, what's she saying got to do with him stealing my Appaloosa?

13:06.200 --> 13:08.200
She's a character witness.

13:08.200 --> 13:11.200
What we need here is a miracle witness.

13:11.200 --> 13:13.200
Order of the court.

13:13.200 --> 13:18.200
Your Honor, may I approach the bench?

13:24.200 --> 13:26.200
That's what I call a good approach to the bench.

13:30.200 --> 13:32.200
Say what you have to say, ma'am.

13:32.200 --> 13:37.200
Well, Your Honor, I'd do just about anything to save Dusty's life.

13:37.200 --> 13:41.200
Marshall, if we're going to get on with hanging this fella,

13:41.200 --> 13:44.200
don't you go getting swayed by no painted lady.

13:45.200 --> 13:46.200
She ain't no painted lady.

13:46.200 --> 13:48.200
She's my friend.

13:48.200 --> 13:51.200
And if you want to be swayed by a friend, the painted lady, just go right ahead.

13:52.200 --> 13:54.200
You can step down now, Miss.

13:57.200 --> 14:04.200
Your Honor, I think it is time that I had a talk with you in the privacy of your chambers.

14:04.200 --> 14:07.200
I ain't got no chambers. Speak your mind.

14:07.200 --> 14:10.200
Well, it's a terribly personal. It concerns...

14:10.200 --> 14:12.200
Are you offering me a bribe?

14:12.200 --> 14:14.200
A bribe? How dare you, sir?

14:14.200 --> 14:16.200
Well, if you are, you're wasting your money.

14:16.200 --> 14:19.200
I was merely willing to offer a very great deal of money

14:19.200 --> 14:23.200
to have you release this young man on bail permanently.

14:23.200 --> 14:26.200
God, you would never dream of bribing anyone.

14:26.200 --> 14:29.200
It still sounded like a bribe to me.

14:30.200 --> 14:32.200
Let me approach it in a little bit.

14:32.200 --> 14:35.200
Let me approach it in a different way.

14:35.200 --> 14:39.200
I am willing to pay a large amount of money to this young man here

14:39.200 --> 14:43.200
for the misappropriated horse, providing it spares Dusty's life.

14:43.200 --> 14:45.200
Thanks a lot, Mr. Brookhaven.

14:45.200 --> 14:47.200
The horse ain't for sale, mister.

14:47.200 --> 14:49.200
No matter how much money you got.

14:49.200 --> 14:52.200
Nonsense! Every man has his price.

14:52.200 --> 14:53.200
Women, too!

14:53.200 --> 14:54.200
Your Honor.

14:54.200 --> 14:55.200
Order in the court!

14:55.200 --> 14:58.200
Sit down, mister. You've had your piece?

14:58.200 --> 15:00.200
Has anybody else got anything to say before I pass judgment?

15:00.200 --> 15:02.200
I do.

15:02.200 --> 15:04.200
That man is guilty.

15:04.200 --> 15:05.200
Right.

15:05.200 --> 15:08.200
Oh, I mean, he is guilty of making a simple mistake.

15:08.200 --> 15:11.200
If Dusty had thought for a minute that horse belonged to somebody else,

15:11.200 --> 15:14.200
he'd have never claimed it for his own.

15:14.200 --> 15:18.200
Well, you and I both know we all make stupid mistakes from time to time.

15:18.200 --> 15:20.200
I sure do.

15:20.200 --> 15:21.200
Just like you're doing now.

15:21.200 --> 15:22.200
Right.

15:22.200 --> 15:25.200
I should have been the one to find that brand, but I didn't.

15:25.200 --> 15:27.200
So it's my fault.

15:27.200 --> 15:30.200
And I'm asking you to hang me instead.

15:30.200 --> 15:32.200
You don't have to take my blame.

15:32.200 --> 15:35.200
Marshal, we found the accused sitting on my horse, not him.

15:35.200 --> 15:37.200
And that's a hard fact.

15:37.200 --> 15:41.200
Under the circumstances, I ain't got but one choice.

15:41.200 --> 15:44.200
And that's to find you, the defendant, guilty.

15:44.200 --> 15:46.200
Oh, no!

15:46.200 --> 15:48.200
Son! Order in the court!

15:48.200 --> 15:50.200
I'm afraid we're gonna have to hang you, son.

15:50.200 --> 15:53.200
What are you afraid about? I'm the one who's gonna be hung.

15:53.200 --> 15:55.200
So hang him at setup.

15:55.200 --> 15:58.200
It only gives me about 12 hours to fix that telegraph.

15:58.200 --> 16:00.200
What good's that gonna do us now?

16:00.200 --> 16:03.200
They're the Territorial Court of Appeals in Johnson City.

16:03.200 --> 16:05.200
If I can get the judge there to declare a mistrial,

16:05.200 --> 16:07.200
the marshal will have to free Dusty.

16:07.200 --> 16:10.200
Come on, let's shackle him up. Take him over there.

16:10.200 --> 16:12.200
Court's adjourned!

16:15.200 --> 16:17.200
Now, you can sleep in this tonight.

16:17.200 --> 16:20.200
Well, considering the hanging and everything, I don't like the shape of my bed.

16:20.200 --> 16:23.200
Well, this way nobody'll have to keep guard.

16:23.200 --> 16:26.200
And everybody'll get a good night's rest. Now, get in there.

16:26.200 --> 16:32.200
There's no way he's gonna run away, changing this fancy voice barrel.

16:36.200 --> 16:39.200
Andy, you go see if you can get that telegraph fixed.

16:39.200 --> 16:42.200
I got an idea that might give us the time we need.

16:42.200 --> 16:54.200
Right.

17:12.200 --> 17:17.200
Hey, Dusty boy.

17:17.200 --> 17:19.200
Dusty.

17:19.200 --> 17:20.200
Wait.

17:20.200 --> 17:22.200
I got the key.

17:22.200 --> 17:24.200
Here.

17:24.200 --> 17:25.200
You unlock this one.

17:25.200 --> 17:26.200
You unlock that one.

17:26.200 --> 17:42.200
I gotta get my guns.

17:56.200 --> 17:57.200
You okay, Dusty?

17:57.200 --> 18:00.200
Yeah, I guess so. That handcuff was really tight.

18:00.200 --> 18:02.200
That handcuff really hurts when you got it around your...

18:02.200 --> 18:03.200
You'll wake up the marshal.

18:03.200 --> 18:05.200
You don't believe me. I'll show you. Look.

18:05.200 --> 18:08.200
Just like that, see? It hurts, huh?

18:08.200 --> 18:13.200
I think the marshal's waking up.

18:13.200 --> 18:14.200
Oh, no.

18:14.200 --> 18:15.200
It's me, I want my handcuff.

18:15.200 --> 18:18.200
I'm gonna... I'm gonna be killed before I get home.

18:18.200 --> 18:26.200
No, it's all right.

18:26.200 --> 18:27.200
I'll go back to sleep again.

18:27.200 --> 18:31.200
Okay, take these off.

18:31.200 --> 18:33.200
I did give you the keys, didn't I?

18:33.200 --> 18:34.200
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

18:34.200 --> 18:35.200
Yeah, good.

18:35.200 --> 18:36.200
But...

18:36.200 --> 18:37.200
But what?

18:37.200 --> 18:38.200
But...

18:38.200 --> 18:39.200
I threw them away over there.

18:39.200 --> 18:49.200
If we get out of this, I may hang you myself.

18:49.200 --> 19:12.200
Oh, gee.

19:12.200 --> 19:32.200
You folks know the penalty for aiding and abetting the escape of a horse thief?

19:32.200 --> 19:34.200
We didn't aid and abet anyone.

19:34.200 --> 19:36.200
Well, I would have if I could have.

19:36.200 --> 19:39.200
We would have if we could have, and we should have.

19:39.200 --> 19:41.200
The wagon master sprung him loose.

19:41.200 --> 19:54.200
Looks like when we catch up to him, we'll have a double-neck tie party.

19:54.200 --> 19:56.200
Don't warn me when you're gonna stop.

19:56.200 --> 19:58.200
I'm sorry.

19:58.200 --> 20:00.200
Stop!

20:00.200 --> 20:04.200
Is that fast enough?

20:04.200 --> 20:05.200
Hey, Dusty, do you know where we are?

20:05.200 --> 20:07.200
Yeah, sure do, up the creek.

20:07.200 --> 20:09.200
No, no, this is the place you found that apple lusa.

20:09.200 --> 20:10.200
Oh, no, let's get out of here.

20:10.200 --> 20:11.200
I don't want to find another one.

20:11.200 --> 20:12.200
I'll get hung twice.

20:12.200 --> 20:14.200
No, no, if we can find another set of hoof prints,

20:14.200 --> 20:16.200
it might lead us to the real horse thief.

20:16.200 --> 20:19.200
And it was split up so we can cover more ground that way.

20:19.200 --> 20:20.200
Right.

20:20.200 --> 20:21.200
Oh, good.

20:21.200 --> 20:25.200
Wait, we have got to find something to get these things off of us.

20:25.200 --> 20:26.200
Not a chance.

20:26.200 --> 20:29.200
These handcuffs are as solid as a rock.

20:29.200 --> 20:34.200
Well, keep looking, okay?

20:34.200 --> 20:35.200
Can't see anything.

20:35.200 --> 20:37.200
Neither can I.

20:37.200 --> 20:40.200
Well, I guess we're still gonna be stuck together for the rest of our lives.

20:40.200 --> 20:43.200
I guess so.

20:43.200 --> 20:46.200
Hey, how'd you do that?

20:46.200 --> 20:48.200
How did I...

20:48.200 --> 20:49.200
How did I do that?

20:49.200 --> 20:50.200
Never mind, never mind.

20:50.200 --> 20:53.200
When we're old and sitting in rocking chairs, we'll figure it out.

20:53.200 --> 20:56.200
But we will never live to get old if we don't find that horse thief.

20:56.200 --> 20:58.200
I'll tell you what.

20:58.200 --> 20:59.200
You take that trail.

20:59.200 --> 21:01.200
I'll go down that way.

21:01.200 --> 21:03.200
If either one of us spot anything, we meet back here.

21:03.200 --> 21:10.200
All right?

21:10.200 --> 21:12.200
Well, take it off, young fella.

21:12.200 --> 21:14.200
Some folks like to die with their boots on.

21:14.200 --> 21:21.200
Not me.

21:21.200 --> 21:24.200
Please reconsider what you're doing.

21:24.200 --> 21:26.200
Hey, hold it, hang it, hold it, hang it.

21:26.200 --> 21:28.200
Here's your horse thief right here.

21:28.200 --> 21:30.200
It's Crazy Blue.

21:30.200 --> 21:31.200
Crazy Blue?

21:31.200 --> 21:34.200
That's the wild stallion that's been chasing horses off all over the territory.

21:34.200 --> 21:36.200
Oh, I thought he was dead.

21:36.200 --> 21:38.200
He's been around these parts for years.

21:38.200 --> 21:42.200
Yeah, well, he's driven some of your prized stock into a box canyon about four miles from here.

21:42.200 --> 21:44.200
He could have driven off that Appaloosa of yours, too.

21:44.200 --> 21:46.200
Well, yeah.

21:46.200 --> 21:48.200
I suppose he could have.

21:48.200 --> 21:51.200
Well, now, I reckon we almost made a dumb mistake.

21:51.200 --> 21:52.200
You are free to go, sonny.

21:52.200 --> 21:57.200
I know, I know.

21:57.200 --> 21:58.200
Mr. Callahan?

21:58.200 --> 22:00.200
I don't know how to say thank you except...

22:00.200 --> 22:01.200
Thank you.

22:01.200 --> 22:02.200
Oh, that's all right, little pal.

22:02.200 --> 22:04.200
You'd have done anything in the world to save my neck, wouldn't you?

22:04.200 --> 22:11.200
I'd save your whole body.

22:11.200 --> 22:13.200
Oh, Freckles.

22:13.200 --> 22:25.200
I love you.

22:25.200 --> 22:27.200
No, I can't take Freckles away.

22:27.200 --> 22:28.200
He's my horse.

22:28.200 --> 22:30.200
And I love him.

22:30.200 --> 22:31.200
No?

22:31.200 --> 22:32.200
No.

22:32.200 --> 22:33.200
No, no, no, no.

22:33.200 --> 22:35.200
You're carrying me, Freckles.

22:35.200 --> 22:38.200
You're having that same crazy dream again.

22:38.200 --> 22:44.200
Yeah, about the sheriff and the rancher and the hanging and the yig and all the roo.

22:44.200 --> 22:47.200
But he's gonna take Freckles away from you.

22:47.200 --> 22:50.200
He was a wild horse and you broke him.

22:50.200 --> 22:52.200
And he belongs to you.

22:52.200 --> 22:54.200
Yeah.

22:54.200 --> 22:55.200
Why?

22:55.200 --> 23:00.200
Because then I could be having a nightmare.

23:00.200 --> 23:29.200
Good night, baby.

23:30.200 --> 23:37.200
Good night.

